From d01c20ec3aca95bea35a0f83581745ff3ab04abe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:10:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 56/56] drm/gma500: let debugfs size the PB of new sgxfive
 render contexts

The partial-render work needs scenes that overflow the parameter buffer,
and every render context had the closed driver's 0x422-page PB with fixed
thresholds. With a PBSize hint the closed driver builds a 0x62-page PB,
and both of its sizes follow one rule: TA threshold = pages + 0x10, ZLS
and global thresholds = pages - 0x22, PDS threshold = global - 0x100 when
positive, else 0.

sgx_render_pb() now takes the page count and derives the thresholds by
that rule; counts outside 0x23-0x422 (the smallest with a ZLS threshold,
the slot's PB) give the whole PB. debugfs dri/N/sgx/render_pb_pages sets
the count for render contexts created afterwards and for the debugfs
triangle, and DEV_QUERY reports the count in effect. The default is
unchanged.

KUnit checks the closed driver's small PB word for word, the page chain,
and the accepted range.

Assisted-by: LLM
